00:06:18.993 --> 00:06:24.893
Australia, co-host of the COP-31 United Nations Climate Talks in Turkey, put out a draft

00:06:24.893 --> 00:06:27.633
on Thursday that drops any mention of fossil fuels.

00:06:28.233 --> 00:06:34.193
France 24 reports, nearly 200 countries have until Friday for a final text, though these

00:06:34.193 --> 00:06:35.513
meetings often run long.

00:06:36.113 --> 00:06:41.053
Deutsche Welles says the talks have been in Antalya since November 9th that an earlier draft

00:06:41.053 --> 00:06:46.353
this week still included a fossil fuel phase out, and that Thursday night's text leaves out gas,

00:06:46.693 --> 00:06:53.173
oil, and coal. France 24 places the summit against a record El Niño, climate-linked disasters

00:06:53.173 --> 00:07:00.073
from Europe to Nepal, and an energy shock from the Iran War. Three years ago, at COP28 in Dubai,

00:07:00.753 --> 00:07:06.793
countries pledged to move away from fossil fuels with no date and no target. Last year's COP30 in

00:07:06.793 --> 00:07:08.533
Brazil ended without mentioning them.

00:07:09.113 --> 00:07:13.393
Oil and gas producing countries have strongly resisted putting the issue back on the table.

00:07:14.093 --> 00:07:19.273
Francis Ecological Transition Minister Monique Barboot called the omission a black mark.

00:07:19.873 --> 00:07:25.373
Harjeet Singh of the Phil the Fun Campaign said you cannot solve a fossil fuel crisis by pretending

00:07:25.373 --> 00:07:26.793
a phase out is unnecessary.

00:07:27.613 --> 00:07:32.173
Muhammad Adau of PowerShift Africa said the thinner text had gone backwards.

00:07:32.173 --> 00:07:37.653
words. Their case is that naming coal, oil and gas is the honest line because those fuels

00:07:37.653 --> 00:07:42.453
drive the heating. The producing countries recorded position is refusal to reopen a

00:07:42.453 --> 00:07:47.633
phase out Dubai left undated. Chris Bowen, Australia's climate minister and the lead

00:07:47.633 --> 00:07:53.153
negotiator said they will keep consulting until it is clear they have a consensus. That rule

00:07:53.153 --> 00:07:58.113
is how a sentence present in one draft can vanish from the next. Whether Friday's text

00:07:58.113 --> 00:08:01.433
or an overtime text puts the fuels back in is the check.

