00:12:15.604 --> 00:12:20.524
To really understand a climate draft that names or erases fossil fuels, you have to separate

00:12:20.524 --> 00:12:23.124
the electricity socket from the whole energy system.

00:12:28.684 --> 00:12:33.724
In 2015, governments in Paris agreed to do what they could to stop the world overheating.

00:12:34.104 --> 00:12:38.824
Since then, coal, oil, and gas have fallen to a record low share of primary energy,

00:12:39.204 --> 00:12:45.404
meaning all energy supplied, not only electricity, and they still make up around 86% of that supply.

00:12:45.884 --> 00:12:51.104
Mark Maslin, an Earth-system scientist at University College London, told Deutschewella

00:12:51.104 --> 00:12:53.584
we are still burning stuff like the 19th century.

00:12:54.444 --> 00:12:55.504
Electricity moved faster.

00:12:56.084 --> 00:13:01.244
Wind, solar, and hydropower were around 34% of global electricity in 2025.

00:13:02.064 --> 00:13:07.164
An Ember analysis found record solar growth last year, let clean energy meet all new

00:13:07.164 --> 00:13:10.564
electricity demand, which held back new fossil generation.

00:13:11.184 --> 00:13:16.524
Maslin put investment in new renewable projects at about $2 trillion dollars, twice the money

00:13:16.524 --> 00:13:17.704
going into fossil fuels.

00:13:17.704 --> 00:13:22.664
The United Nations now says overshooting the Paris temperature threshold is inevitable,

00:13:23.124 --> 00:13:27.264
and that the time above it should be as short as possible, with heating brought back

00:13:27.264 --> 00:13:32.484
down by the end of the century, because a longer overshoot raises the chance of self-reinforcing

00:13:32.484 --> 00:13:35.924
shifts such as large forest dye back and melting permafrost.

00:13:36.444 --> 00:13:41.544
Next time a summit line says phase out or stays silent, ask whether the number beside it

00:13:41.544 --> 00:13:43.384
is primary energy or electricity.

